		"tagline": "Two weeks, four people, tasks keep coming. You decide what kind of lead to be.",
		"rules": "[b]How to play[/b]\n• Tasks arrive every day. Click a task, then a person — it's theirs. If they have a reason to refuse (swamped, exhausted, hate this kind of work, not good at it), they'll push back and you'll have to talk them round. Tasks queue up for that person — they do one at a time, nearest deadline first.\n• You don't know who's good at what or what drives them. You learn it from their results and in one-on-ones (one talk a day).\n• A task can get a helper: they give it half a day (a whole day if they have nothing of their own). A stronger one speeds it up, a weaker one learns.\n• There's more work than the team can handle. Decide what matters: Irina notices her own overdue tasks at once, others won't complain to her the first time.\n• Watch mood and energy: overload leads to sick leave, resentment to resignation.\n• Every Friday: the week's report (who worked how much) and Irina's review: you decide who gets the credit and who takes the blame.\n• You can do everything yourself, or nothing at all. Your call.",
